From: CEB-GNRD maintainers <bmc@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] virtual-media: retain browser mounts across menu navigation

Keep the VirtualMedia route instance alive for the authenticated application
and use a stable key when changing menus or refreshing other views. Recheck
device metadata when returning without replacing the objects captured by NBD
callbacks. Retain connecting sockets, avoid wrapping NBD in a reactive proxy,
and stop local sockets on logout or application teardown. Explicit Stop and
the existing NBD read verification and transport error handling remain active.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CEB-GNRD browser virtual media]
---

--- a/src/layouts/AppLayout.vue
+++ b/src/layouts/AppLayout.vue
@@ -10,7 +10,15 @@
     />
     <app-navigation :key="routerKey" class="app-navigation" />
     <page-container class="app-content">
-      <router-view ref="routerView" :key="routerKey" />
+      <router-view v-slot="{ Component, route }">
+        <keep-alive include="VirtualMedia">
+          <component
+            :is="Component"
+            ref="routerView"
+            :key="route.name === 'virtual-media' ? 'virtual-media' : routerKey"
+          />
+        </keep-alive>
+      </router-view>
       <!-- Scroll to top button -->
       <button-back-to-top />
     </page-container>
